nd 3D printing for rapid prototyping -> /about", "Deep understanding of electrical measurements -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Ohio Semitronics pioneered and developed the first Hall Effect electrical measurement devices.", "founded_year": "1964", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ohio-semitronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ohio Shirt Company operates from Findlay, Ohio, where it maintains an appointment-only showroom at PO Box 88. The company sells directly to consumers through its e-commerce website, offering a range of Ohio-themed printed apparel.

The product line centers on screen-printed and decorated garments such as T-shirts, hoodies, and crew-neck sweatshirts featuring Ohio scripts, football motifs, and retro designs. Prices range from $25 for a basic tee to $39 for hoodies, with occasional sale pricing. The company promotes free shipping on orders exceeding $100.

