UPDATE companies SET description='Ohio Woodworking Company operates from a facility near downtown Cincinnati, Ohio, on the same site where German immigrant William Frank founded the business in 1930 after apprenticing as a cabinetmaker. Now a third-generation, family-owned firm, leadership has passed from Frank to his son Tom and then to Tom’s son Tom Jr. and son-in-law Richard, who together bring over 27 years of cabinetmaking expertise.

The shop combines CNC machinery and AutoCAD-based drafting with traditional woodworking tools to produce custom millwork and cabinetry for commercial and institutional spaces. Capabilities range from one-of-a-kind custom builds to large-scale production runs, covering architectural millwork, commercial casework, retail fixtures, bank teller lines, salon displays, university furniture, residential cabinetry, and kitchen and food service stations. A dedicated team—many with decades of experience—supports the full design-to-execution process alongside architects, designers, and trades.

The company serves banking, retail, salon, higher education, medical office, and food service sectors. Long-standing clients include U.S. Bank, which relies on Ohio Woodworking for branch fixtures and casework. Projects also encompass medical office reception areas, salon and service area furniture, and custom residential work, all engineered to precise specifications.

Ohio Woodworking emphasizes values of quality, ingenuity, perseverance, humor, and family—principles the firm says are built into every project. By blending time-tested techniques with modern technology, the company aims to deliver precision, reliability, and smart custom solutions that sustain decades-long partnerships.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom millwork", "Cabinetry", "CNC machining", "AutoCAD drafting", "Architectural millwork", "Commercial casework", "Retail fixture fabrication", "Bank fixture fabrication", "Salon display fabrication", "University furniture fabrication", "Residential cabinetry", "Kitchen and food service station fabrication", "Salon & service area furniture fabrication"], "industries": ["Banking", "Retail", "Salon & personal care", "Higher education", "Medical office", "Food service", "Commercial", "Institutional"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["CNC machinery", "AutoCAD drafting software"], "volume": "One-of-a-kind custom builds to large-scale production runs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Third-generation family ownership since 1930", "Nearly 95 years of continuous operation", "CNC machining and AutoCAD drafting paired with traditional hand tools", "Decades-long client relationships (e.g., U.S. Bank)", "Capacity for both one-off custom pieces and large production runs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1930 by William Frank -> /about", "Third-generation family-owned -> /about, /", "Headquarters Cincinnati, Ohio -> /about, /", "Facility near downtown Cincinnati with CNC and AutoCAD -> /about", "Custom millwork and cabinetry for commercial/institutional -> /", "Services: architectural millwork, commercial casework, retail fixtures, bank fixtures, salon displays, university furniture, residential cabinetry, kitchen/food service stations -> /, db", "Client example: U.S. Bank -> /", "Industries: banking, retail, salon, university, medical office, food service -> /, db", "Values: quality, ingenuity, perseverance, humor, family -> /about", "Handles one-of-a-kind to large-scale production -> /about", "Team with decades of experience -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "deliver high-end custom millwork and cabinetry for commercial and institutional spaces", "founded_year": "1930", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ohio-woodworking-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ohlhauser Custom Woodworx operates from Lincoln, North Dakota.

The shop produces custom furniture, cabinetry, and decorative accents, working with both new and reclaimed lumber such as barnwood. Services include custom CNC milling, personalized engraving, and a range of smaller handcrafted items like cutting boards, turkey fan mounts, key racks, and novelty gifts. The company describes its output as handcrafted, high-quality wood products tailored to client specifications.

Customers include homeowners and commercial clients in the Bismarck region seeking bespoke pieces for residences, offices, and other spaces. Projects referenced range from residential furniture and cabinetry to commercial installations and personalized gift items.

