UPDATE companies SET description='P1 Technologies operates from a 144,000-square-foot vertically integrated facility in Roanoke, Virginia. The company traces its roots to 1949 and was rebranded as P1 Technologies in 2019. It is employee-owned.

The company provides turnkey contract manufacturing services including printed circuit board assembly (PCBA), box builds, additive manufacturing, rapid prototyping, custom cable assemblies, in-house tooling design and fabrication, precision molding, packaging, inspection, and cleanroom sterile barrier packaging. With two SMT production lines equipped with Europlacer pick-and-place machines, the facility supports surface-mount, through-hole, BGA and micro-BGA assembly, selective soldering, automated conformal coating, and rework. The operation runs from prototype through full production volumes with a staff of over 480.

P1 serves original equipment manufacturers in the medical, defense, and audio sectors. Medical work includes diagnostic connectors and sterile-packaged assemblies; defense programs require rugged interconnects for mission-critical conditions; audio customers rely on high-end cable assemblies for professional and in-ear-monitor applications.

The company emphasizes its integrated in-house model as a differentiator, citing lean operations that reduce waste, deep supply-chain knowledge that shortens lead times, and advanced capabilities that keep control, speed, and reliability under one roof. It holds ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 13485:2016 certifications, is FDA registered, and ITAR compliant.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485:2016','FDA Registered','ITAR Compliant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCBA (printed circuit board assembly)", "Box builds", "Additive manufacturing", "Rapid prototyping", "Custom cable assemblies & connectors", "In-house tooling design & fabrication", "Precision molding", "Packaging & inspection", "Cleanroom & sterile barrier packaging", "Surface mount technology (SMT) assembly", "Through-hole assembly", "BGA and micro-BGA assembly", "Selective soldering", "Automated conformal coating", "Rework and repair", "Final assembly testing", "Ultra-precise part fabrication"], "industries": ["Medical", "Defense", "Audio"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Europlacer pick-and-place equipment", "SMT production lines"], "volume": "Prototype to production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house tooling design and fabrication", "ISO Class 7 & 8 cleanroom capabilities for sterile barrier packaging", "Additive manufacturing and soft tooling for rapid prototyping", "Turnkey assembly and inspection from PCB integration to final validation", "ISO 9001:2015, ISO 13485:2016, FDA registered, ITAR compliant"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1949 -> /about-us", "Rebranded as P1 Technologies in 2019 -> /about-us", "Employee-owned -> /about-us", "Headquarters Roanoke, Virginia -> / (homepage) and /about-us", "Facility size 144,000 sq ft -> / (homepage) and /about-us", "Employee count 480+ -> /about-us", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, ISO 13485:2016, FDA Registered, ITAR Compliant -> /about-us", "ROHS certification -> db", "Capabilities: PCBA, box builds, additive manufacturin