UPDATE companies SET description='PMC SMART Solutions, headquartered in Shelbyville, Indiana, traces its origins to 1929 when two families founded Plastic Moldings Company in Cincinnati, Ohio, during the Great Depression. The business remains privately owned by the founding family, now led by fourth‑generation President and CEO Lisa Jennings, and earned WBE and WOSB certification in 2013.

The company specializes in complex engineering and technical solutions for difficult‑to‑mold, high‑temperature components. Its core capabilities include high‑temperature and implantable biomaterials injection molding, hyper‑precision and insert molding to micron tolerances, scientific injection molding, insert and over‑molding, design and engineering services, and complete secondary operations and assembly, delivering finished medical devices and automotive components.

PMC serves the medical device and automotive industries, counting global OEMs such as Medtronic and Bosch among its strategic customers. Its medical portfolio spans development through assembly of life‑saving products, while its automotive work emphasizes hyper‑precision molding and contract assembly for safety‑critical systems.

The firm differentiates itself through a quality system that has achieved first‑time certification on four registered standards and a 100 % success rate in external audits. Its SMART Solutions™ framework combines engineering, design, molding, and assembly under a culture of accountability, innovation, and stewardship, aiming to make customers’ products safer, stronger, and more affordable.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485','IATF 16949','CFR 21.820','WBE','WOSB']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["High-temperature and implantable biomaterials injection molding", "Hyper-precision molding and insert molding (to micron tolerances)", "Design & Engineering Services", "Scientific Injection Molding", "Injection molding \u2013 insert and over-molding", "Complete secondary operation and assembly services", "Finished device manufacturing and assembly", "Technology development", "Quality systems (ISO 13485, IATF 16949, CFR 21.820 compliance)", "Contract assembly"], "industries": ["Medical device", "Automotive"], "materials": ["High-temperature biomaterials", "Implantable biomaterials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "Micron tolerances", "built_on": ["Hyper\u2011precision molding and insert molding to micron tolerances", "High\u2011temperature and implantable biomaterials injection molding expertise", "Scientific injection molding methodology", "Complete secondary operations and assembly services", "100\u202f% external audit success with first\u2011time certification on four quality standards"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1929 in Cincinnati, Ohio -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Shelbyville, Indiana -> db", "Privately owned by founding family, fourth-generation, led by Lisa Jennings -> /about-us", "WBE and WOSB certified in 2013 -> /about-us", "ISO 13485 and IATF 16949 certified -> /quality and db", "CFR 21.820 compliance -> /quality", "Capabilities: high-temperature and implantable biomaterials injection molding, hyper-precision molding to mic