UPDATE companies SET description='Paricon Technologies Corporation operates from Taunton, Massachusetts, where it designs and manufactures elastomeric interconnect solutions for the electronics industry.

The company''s core offering centers on its PariPoser® anisotropic elastomer fabric, a material engineered for bandwidths exceeding 110 GHz that behaves as a lumped parameter with inductance below 0.1 nH. Paricon translates this technology into a range of interconnect products including die-cut material, adjustable swivel-top sockets, clamshell sockets, compact manual-loading sockets, double-latch sockets, flex-to-board assemblies, and board-to-board connectors. It also provides PariProbe® probe solutions that combine elastomers with short solid pins for BGA applications, supported by optional Peltier or liquid cooling for thermal management.

Paricon serves customers in test and measurement, microwave and RF, wafer testing, custom connector applications, and high-speed digital electronics. Its solutions are used in applications requiring reliable high-frequency contacts, such as RF waveguides, large BGA probing, and advanced semiconductor test.

The company states its mission is to deliver innovative elastomeric interconnect solutions that enable customers to push the boundaries of electronics design and manufacturing. Its vision targets global leadership in high-performance interconnects, grounded in core values of innovation, quality, customer focus, and excellence. Paricon emphasizes continuous R&D investment in proprietary technologies to stay ahead of industry needs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design and manufacture of elastomeric interconnect solutions", "Die cutting of anisotropic elastomer fabric", "Socket assembly (adjustable swivel-top, clamshell, compact manual-loading, double-latch, flex-to-board, board-to-board)", "PariPoser\u00ae anisotropic elastomer fabric production", "PariProbe\u00ae probe solutions for BGA applications", "Thermal management integration (Peltier and liquid cooling)"], "industries": ["Test and measurement", "Microwave and RF", "Wafer testing", "Custom connector applications", "High-speed digital electronics", "Semiconductor test"], "materials": ["Anisotropic elastomer fabric (PariPoser\u00ae)", "Elastomer", "Short solid pins (for PariProbe\u00ae)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Taunton, Massachusetts -> db", "Designer and manufacturer of elastomeric interconnect solutions -> /about-us", "PariPoser\u00ae anisotropic elastomer fabric with bandwidth above 110 GHz -> /about-us", "PariProbe\u00ae technology for BGA probing with thermal management -> /about-us", "Products include die-cut material, various socket assemblies, flex-to-board, board-to-board -> /", "Industries served: test, microwave, wafer testing, custom connector applications -> /about-us", "Mission and vision statements -> /about-us", "Core values: Innovation, Quality, Customer Focus, Excellence -> /about-us", "Electrical performance: lumped parameter below 100 GHz, <0.1 nH inductance -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Paricon Technologies Corporation is a leading designer, manufacturer, and marketer of state-of-the-art elastomeric interconnect solutions", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='paricon-technologies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Park Distributors Inc. was founded in 1966 in Bridgeport, Connecticut.

The firm operates as a global wholesale distributor of electronic and electrical components, maintaining franchised relationships with manufacturers such as Datatel, Middle Atlantic Products, Surge Components, Master Appliance, OK Industries, Electrotek, and Esico. Beyond distribution, Park provides value-added services including cable and harness assembly, just-in-time delivery, and kitting. The company also specializes in hard-to-find and custom-designed relays, claiming the largest stock of diversified relays in the United States.

The company states that its founding purpose was to deliver quality, competitive pricing, and service in the marketplace, selecting only product lines that complement that function. Its differentiation rests on the breadth of its relay inventory, franchised manufacturer partnerships, and the ability to provide custom relay solutions alongside standard distribution.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cable & harness assembly", "Just-in-time (JIT) delivery", "Kitting", "Custom relay design", "Franchised electronic component distribution"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest stock of diversified relays in the United States", "Franchised distributor for industry-leading manufacturers", "Custom designed relays and hard-to-find components", "Value-added services: cable & harness assembly, JIT delivery, kitting"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1966 -> db, /about", "Headquarters Bridgeport, CT -> /about", "Global wholesale distributor of electronic components -> /about", "Largest stock of diversified relays in US -> /about", "Franchised lines from manufacturers like Datatel, Master Appliance, OK Industries -> /about", "Value-added services: cable & harness assembly, JIT, kitting -> /about, products", "Custom designed relays -> /about", "Offers hard-to-find relays -> /about"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "unclear", "type_evidence": "Park Distributors, Inc. is a global wholesale distributor of electronic and electronic components.", "founded_year": "1966", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='park-distributors-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Parkman Woodworks was founded in 2015 on Parkman Avenue in Silverlake, Los Angeles, by Graham Taglang, who remains the public face of the company. The venture began with a pickup truck and a thousand dollars, building its first pieces from sustainable wood in a friend''s driveway. In 2019 the operation moved into a historic brick-and-timber textile mill a building that marked its 100th anniversary in 2023, with a roof framed in the same antique timber the shop uses for furniture.

The company produces custom wood-and-steel furniture—conference tables, dining tables, bed frames, desks, coffee tables, bookshelves, consoles, benches, mantels, countertops, and restaurant pieces—entirely in-house. A team of six craftspeople handles design, woodworking, welding, and powder-coating of low-carbon iron, working from the 100-year-old facility. Materials are sourced hyperlocally: solid hardwoods recovered from naturally fallen Southern California trees and structures.

Parkman serves both residential and commercial clients. Its furniture furnishes corporate offices, home offices, dining rooms, bedrooms, kitchens, living rooms, and restaurants.

The founding mission is to turn wasted wood into practical art while advancing the values of handcraft. The shop emphasizes accountability, awareness, and achievement, with every piece passing through the full in-house build process from design to delivery.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Woodworking", "Welding/ironworking", "Powder coating", "In-house fabrication", "Live edge furniture construction", "Wood charring", "Cabinet and drawer making", "Conference table manufacturing", "Dining table manufacturing", "Bed frame manufacturing", "Desk manufacturing", "Coffee table manufacturing", "Bookshelf manufacturing", "Console and casegoods manufacturing", "Bench manufacturing", "Mantel and countertop fabrication", "Restaurant furniture manufacturing"], "industries": ["Corporate office", "Restaurant", "Residential"], "materials": ["Solid hardwoods", "Naturally fallen Southern California lumber", "Low-carbon iron", "Powder coating", "Antique timber"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 2015 on Parkman Avenue in Silverlake, Los Angeles -> /about-us", "Moved in 2019 to historic brick-and-timber textile mill at 160 S Mission Rd, Los Angeles, CA 90033 -> /about-us", "Graham Taglang public face since 2015 -> /about-us", "Team members: Kyle Jordan (2018), Jimmy Welsh (2019), Susannah Rea-Downing (2019), Preston Weimer (2020), Randy Zamudio (2022) -> /about-us", "Custom handmade wood & steel furniture -> /", "Hyperlocal sustainably sourced wood from naturally fallen Southern California trees -> /", "In-house fabrication, welding, powder coating -> /about-us", "100-year-old workshop -> /about-us", "Serve corporate office, dining room, bedroom, kitchen, home office, living room, restaurant -> /", "Mission: turn world''s wasted wood into practical art -> /about-us", "Values: Accountability, Awareness, Achievement -> /about-us", "Phone and hours -> /about-u